        "claim": "Fresh chunks of meat fell from a clear sky over a farm in Bath County, Kentucky, in March 1876.",
        "segment_index": 0,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "The reference confirms that red meat fell from the sky in a 100-by-50-yard area near Olympia Springs in Bath County on March 3, 1876, for several minutes, and notes Charles Fort stated there was no rain.",
        "correction": null
      },
      {
        "claim": "Local residents inspected the fallen meat and two men tasted it, believing it to be beef or venison.",
        "segment_index": 1,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "Scientific American reported that the meat appeared to be beef, but two men who tasted it judged it to be possibly lamb or deer (venison).",
        "correction": null
      },
      {
        "claim": "Microscopic examination by chemists confirmed the samples were animal cartilage, muscle, and lung tissue.",
        "segment_index": 2,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "Microscopic analysis by researchers confirmed the samples contained lung tissue, muscle, cartilage, and connective tissue.",
        "correction": null
      },
      {
